        "original_id": "bbf4b03f-a5d0-539f-b8e0-f002c3d05590",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean Dubuffet\n- Bands: Art Brut, Franz Ferdinand, The Rakes, Bloc Party, Dananananaykroyd\n- Concepts: outsider art, Art Wave\n- Places: South London, Glasgow\n- Albums: You Could Have It So Much Better, Hey Everyone!\n- Organizations: NME, Best Before Records\n\nFacts:\n- Jean Dubuffet defined outsider art as art by prisoners, loners, mentally ill people, and other marginalized people, made without thought to imitation or presentation.\n- Franz Ferdinand are a Scottish rock band formed in 2002 and based in Glasgow.\n- NME tagged South London's Art Brut as part of the Art Wave scene alongside bands such as The Rakes, Franz Ferdinand, and Bloc Party.\n- You Could Have It So Much Better is the second studio album by Scottish indie rock band Franz Ferdinand.\n- Hey Everyone! is the debut album by Glasgow-based rock band Dananananaykroyd, released on April 6, 2009, on Best Before Records.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
